==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Clearing F_LeastPrivilege removes the role/operation gate. The injected witness is a successful GetAudit call by a customer-role caller, which is explicitly denied by the permission matrix; LeastPrivilege should detect this.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_004_ComplianceReadOnly, FR_021_NoAuditForCustomer
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReadOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_021_NoAuditForCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditFromOp  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditFromOp.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditFromOp lets an AuditEntry exist without any creating Operation — i.e., an entry that was 'forged' or rewritten with no provenance, which is exactly the append-only violation we want to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_StateChangingProducesAudit  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_StateChangingProducesAudit.als
    rationale: Clearing F_StateChangingProducesAudit lets a successful submission complete without writing an audit entry. The injected witness forces exactly that, so AuditCompleteness must report a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_009_SubmitAudit, FR_019_OneAuditPerChange
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_SubmitAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_OneAuditPerChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CustomerOwnership  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_CustomerOwnership.als
    rationale: Clearing F_CustomerOwnership permits a customer to successfully GET an application owned by a different customer; the ownership-based-access invariant should detect this leak.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage, FR_020_CustomerOwnOnly
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_CustomerOwnOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecideRequiresAssigned  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecideRequiresAssigned.als
    rationale: Clearing F_DecideRequiresAssigned removes the only fact that binds the deciding officer to the assigned officer at the operation layer. Injecting a successful DecideApp whose caller is not the target's assigned officer must produce a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_AssignedDecides
      - FR_013_AssignedDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OneInFlightPerCustomer removes the partial-unique-index analogue. Injecting two distinct in-flight applications for the same customer must be detected by FR_008_OneInFlight.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlight
      - FR_008_OneInFlight: FAIL (expected)

